// Windows resources compiled into the executable
// (`features/application-icon.md`, the Windows half of the platform table).
//
// Without this, the installed `yk-dist-manager.exe` carries no icon of its own:
// the MSI's Icon table gives the Start Menu shortcut and the Programs-and-
// Features row one, but Explorer, a pinned taskbar button, Alt-Tab and the
// window class all read the *executable*, and an executable with no icon
// resource gets the generic one. That is the icon an operator reported missing
// after an install, and it was missing because it was never there — the .ico
// existed only in the installer.
//
// Resource id 1 on purpose: the shell shows the icon with the **lowest**
// numeric id as an executable's icon, so the application's mark has to hold it
// rather than merely be present.
//
// The path is relative to this file, which is how both `rc.exe` and `llvm-rc`
// resolve it, so this stays correct whatever directory the build runs from.
1 ICON "icon.ico"
